    "§9.5.1 Past the cap",
    "§10.1 step 2",
    "§10.4"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-10.1-022"
  ],
  "reentrancy": [
    "routed@cascade"
  ],
  "notes": "max_chain_depth is 1, so the cascade's budget is 10 passes. Every message the loop channel's deliveries send names no room, and the router routes it to room-1, the room the work delivers in: the first ten each draw a pass, their own cascades drawing on the same budget, and are stored; the eleventh delivery sends one from sms2, which room-1 does not bind, and one from sms3, which room-1 binds naming no one. Step 2 attaches sms2 naming its sender and records the sender on sms3's binding, then each message is refused past the budget: nothing of either stored, the attach and the record kept.",
